## Context

A multi-role library management web application designed to simplify daily library operations for both administrators and visitors/members through a clean, browser-based interface.

## Problem

Tracking book collections, validating new members, and monitoring book circulation manually makes it hard for staff to keep catalog availability accurate and for visitors to quickly check whether a book is available.

## My role

Owner: I designed the dual-role workflow (Admin and Visitor), built the PHP backend and MySQL database integration, and deployed the containerized live demo on Vercel.

## As-is analysis

Library workflows split into two core journeys: back-office catalog and member administration by librarians, and self-service catalog discovery and borrowing inquiries by visitors. Separating these interfaces reduces clutter and prevents unauthorized catalog edits.

## Requirements

- Role-based access separating Admin (`admin-login.php`, `admin_dashboard.php`) and Visitor (`index-visitor.php`, `katalog-pengguna.php`) portals.
- Full book catalog management: add, edit, delete, and check book availability (`add_books.php`, `edit_book.php`, `delete_book.php`, `check_books.php`).
- Member approval workflow (`approve_member.php`) and borrowing/return monitoring.
- Book data export capability (`export_data_buku`) for administrative reporting.

## Solution design

The application separates public/member catalog browsing from protected administrative endpoints via `backend_api.php` and `db_connect.php`, keeping book availability queries fast and administrative actions auditable.

## Build

Implemented using PHP, MySQL, Composer dependencies, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, and Docker, deployed at `perpustakaan-demo.vercel.app`. Source code: [github.com/thunderclouds863/manajemen-perpustakaan](https://github.com/thunderclouds863/manajemen-perpustakaan).

## Verification

Verified admin login, book CRUD operations, member approval screens, and visitor catalog browsing in the live demo environment.

## Outcome

Delivered a functional multi-role library management web application with live demo access covering catalog administration, member onboarding, and visitor discovery.

## Reflection

Keeping the visitor catalog uncluttered while centralizing approvals and exports in the admin dashboard made the system practical for both technical and non-technical users.
